\section*{Algebraic K-Theory and Rigidity Conjectures for Discrete Groups}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
Two closed aspherical topological four-manifolds are claimed homotopy equivalent but not homeomorphic, sharing a word-hyperbolic fundamental group; one also admits a self-equivalence outside every homeomorphism homotopy class. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 320, 2026-10-04): Reflected marked chambers retain an odd-cover filling obstruction, and carefully chosen binary label relations eliminate unwanted chamber symmetries. Hyperbolicity and Poincare duality make the outer automorphism group finite, with a controlled normalizer of the realized chamber action. A hypothetical homeomorphism would transport another finite action into that realized subgroup and force an excluded conjugacy.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 320, 2026-10-04): The nonhomeomorphic aspherical pair refutes the Borel-rigidity clause of this broad bundle, but does not decide its idempotent, K-group, signature, FP/FF or higher-dimensional realization clauses.

\subsection{Formal verification}
Family 320 has no Lean scope page in this snapshot; no formalization of these manuscript results is listed.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

